If I am too tired and/or going too fast I will confuse items. Even
though I tend to #adjust a lot to avoid this, there are still items I
read/cycle thru too quickly in my inventory when I'm not paying
attention. Ex.: Wasted a !oholywater when accidentally blessing an
ordinary oil lamp instead of one of the two magic ones I was carrying
(all IDed). Now, this particular example hasn't killed me (yet) but
it's a waste of a useful item I'm sure I'll wish I had later (the game
I've been playing has had a bizarre dearth of potions of any type, so
I can't even make more water)--not to mention I can't make the wish I
wanted to make (I'm not going to rub a magic lamp unless it's blessed.
Might as well use it as a light source).

The impatience of not getting what I want also kills me. I have a bad
habit of wanting artifact weapons ASAP (but I won't wish for them,
usually, because there are other things to wish for) and then ending
up doing something stupid at an altar--usually sacing at a nonaligned
altar and getting killed by a priest because I belatedly realized I
wasn't ready to handle them. I don't do that as much _now_ (YASDs will
teach you if you let them) but I will still get impatient if I can't
find that artifact or all important bag of holding or whatever and do
stupid things to try and obtain items I would probably obtain
eventually if I would just slow down.

I too am a packrat and also need to learn to stash and keep track of
my stashes better. I get annoyed after awhile of wandering up and down
the dungeons to check old places (especially if I have a pet(s) and no
magic whistle). Only now have I discovered it's a good idea to keep
notes as you travel along.

Granted, I've never even ascended once, so the "twice as often" issue
is moot. This probably makes me as lame as you can get in this here
forum. I've played the game for years, but off and on, not
continuously; I know _how_ to ascend; I've seen the endgame through
Xploring and the like. Honestly, my biggest flaw is the fact that I
usually play when sleep deprived. :) Time, Patience, luck, patience,
and patience have yet to be with me. And a good bag of holding. :)

